  "releaseHighlights": "- New tool: GD DRT Pro. A display render built on the gradient solve, with the Records tonal engine. The picture is built from three overlapping film like records and recombined as dye density, so colour gradations stay smooth and the neutral axis stays put.\n- GD DRT Pro: built in looks. Pick Balanced Modernity, Faded Glory or Silver Screen from the Preset menu, or Save, Export and Import your own.\n- GD DRT Pro: White Mode menu. SDR sets 100 nits, and SDR as HDR 203 Nits Diffuse sets 406 nits with the body of the picture at 203.\n- GD DRT Pro: Reference Monitor and Display Encode. Grade on a Gamma 2.4 monitor and switch to PQ or HLG without the look changing character. SDR Monitor White and Black trims to match the monitor you actually grade on.\n- GD DRT Pro: Film Textures (Beta). Film grain and halation picked by gauge (65mm, 35mm or 16mm) with a Grain Strength slider. Off by default.\n- New tool: Theater Light DRT. A projector through dye picture former with per layer trims, Color Timing and per layer MTF.\n- New tool: SD>HD GDR Delivery. Re-targets an SDR grade to a PQ or HLG deliverable, with an optional Rec.709 to Rec.2020 gamut step.\n- Much faster at 4K on Mac. GD DRT Pro went from about 7 fps to about 40 fps on a 4K timeline with the exact same picture.\n- Windows and Linux: Razzle Dazzle, Theater Light, HDR Restore, Structure Metric and the Achromatic Test and Colour Leak views now render on CUDA, and GPU memory is reused between frames for smoother playback.",
